      },
      "natural_statement": "Adversarially audit, verify, or refute OpenAI Manuscript Family 350 (Yau’s nodal bounds: surfaces and higher dimensions.; papers: Sharp nodal length on smooth surfaces; Smooth counterexamples to Yau's nodal upper bound in dimensions three and four; Power-law violations of Yau's nodal upper bound; Lean status: Partially/Comparator formalized (lean/docs/350.md)): either (a) discover and certify an explicit mathematical flaw, sign/orientation error, counterexample to an intermediate lemma, or statement-fidelity/citation gap with a deterministic symbolic/computational certificate (`verify.py` + `exact_certificate.json`), or (b) independently verify, repair, or generalize the manuscript's core mathematical theorem with a standalone machine-checkable certificate certified by the independent Reviewer.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "914ed037f48002864c3c3f06083f5a32a677f12ca31c716b250756a1c589d185"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_SURFACE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every fixed smooth closed connected Riemannian surface, all nonzero real eigenfunctions with positive eigenvalue have nodal length at most C times sqrt(lambda); staged surface introduction thm:main, not certified by the local envelope audit.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "7ef716eb7ae471b2f10da384c491e414375674345071710aefbf7a29891c85ef"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_QUALITATIVE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The qualitative manuscript thm:main and thm:four produce fixed smooth metrics on S^3 arbitrarily C-infinity close to round and on S^2 times T^2 with eigenfunction sequences having unbounded nodal measure divided by sqrt(lambda); this branch remains open.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "ddf00a46cdd076256e75685c91b029b8612ed0db4d5a10052ae4a047c098a3b6"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_POWER_NODAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The power-law manuscript thm:main produces one fixed smooth metric on S^4 times S^1 and eigenfunctions whose nodal measure divided by lambda^(1/2+epsilon_0) tends to infinity for a fixed epsilon_0>0; this nodal branch remains open.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "b697b7801002c5bf74f330cb1b4ae5d4008ddf6b7330759bdb334429bfa1ae62"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_POWER_DOWNSTREAM",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The wave, sign-certificate, exactification, spectral-persistence, limiting-pair and warped-circle arguments preserve a common positive gain exponent; these downstream steps are outside the corrugation mission and remain open.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "394435e02cc9148563067a7dc27b56045314630725b61cdb1e07a2e89375105c"
