    {
      "claim_id": "C_LOCAL_HESSIAN",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For a fixed smooth radial-well pattern, w=s*ell*a*chi*psi(z_transverse/ell) has gradient comparison and a uniform positive admissible Hessian test everywhere on each prepared parent, including vanishing cutoff or well coefficients and all positive parent slopes.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "35d534deedfbf73da3c7a276d3c3ff988f3420d4ec07c90b99f1eda283b36452"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_MASS_SELECTION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "A finite radial-well pattern, fixed cores and parent cutoff can be chosen before preparation constants so that whole closed child cubes are prepared with those same constants at scale ell and carry at least (1+zeta) times the entire old parent gradient mass, for fixed zeta>0.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "41f6f0e4c0a4ee258d452a915f51f3dfa77a4d09dfaffc19ff0684e814eb8884"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_CORRUGATION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The literal Lemma lem:corrugation in the staged power-law envelopes.tex holds with every preparation, compact support, gradient, positive-test, closed-child mass-gain and all-order increment condition and with the stated order of parameter choices; no input derivative beyond its prepared Hessian bound is used.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "2534b109a8a245169511de8ad56514d8cfaea9f27597783afa8028206a62e60f"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_ITERATION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The local lemma iterates with I_m>=(1+zeta)^m*I0, all-order norms <=C_j*exp(Cstar*(j+1)*m) for one Cstar independent of j, and Hessian margin >=c*exp(-Cstar*m); a fixed logarithmic generation count yields a positive exponent independent of later accuracy orders.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "1b9a40d1b124de300f39ef61ff8b027f243ad6e1c885213bb2f66fe41036d879"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_ENVELOPE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The literal Proposition prop:envelope holds: with delta=10^-6, one gamma>0 works for every fixed derivative order and later finite accuracy requirement, giving ||h_k||Cj<=C_j*k^(delta*(j+1)), positive-test margin >=c*k^-delta, and integral_V sqrt(1+|grad_G h_k|^2)>=c*k^gamma; corrugations have the prescribed support and bounded constant shifts are allowed.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "7dd8051fec1341f969eb4e2432178a38c3ebd8267b870cfc0402bce6df5a098c"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_CONVEX_AMPLIFICATION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CORRUGATION",
        "content_hash": "819873de68a9539e5792f403e5ae4ebca0fa113b184fe8b32c0390e1f69a5c3a"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every fixed base dimension n>=4 and fixed metric ellipticity/C1 bounds, one radial-well pattern preserves every condition of the corrugation lemma and selects gradients at least rho>1 times the maximum old parent gradient, where the pattern, zeta>0 and rho are chosen before preparation constants and final reciprocal nu. The same modification and closed children simultaneously satisfy integral_R |grad v|^r >= (1+zeta)*rho^(r-1)*integral_P |grad h|^r for every real r>=1 and integral_R Phi(|grad v|)>=(1+zeta)*integral_P Phi(|grad h|) for every finite nonnegative convex Phi with Phi(0)=0. On the S4 seed, one logarithmic iteration gives moment exponents gamma_r=theta*(log(1+zeta)+(r-1)*log(rho)), with theta independent of derivative, moment and later approximation orders. Literature-wide novelty and publishability are not asserted by the Engineer.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "d31b338cf41210e91fda875362ce50e01de284967fb06b124362b5b6f74e03fb"
    }
